Z||000000||Silver Bullet||12-30-1999||12:49 AM||||I have an 85 se (V6) and would like to change the nose of it to maybe an 85 GT nose.  I was wondering if the fascias were interchangeable?  If not, how hard would it be to make it so it was?  I did notice that my car has the marker light on the nose, and I don't think the one that I want does.  Tell me what you think.||||reg||1
Z||000001||TOM||12-30-1999||01:01 AM||||All fascias will work on all cars. You will need the reinforce stuff under the fascia to go with whatever one you want||||reg||1
Z||000002||TOM||12-30-1999||01:01 AM||||All fascias will work on all cars. You will need the reinforce stuff under the fascia to go with whatever one you want||||reg||1
Z||000003||TOM||12-30-1999||01:02 AM||||oops. One post for the front and one for the back. yeah thats it||||reg||1
Z||000004||fieroshop||12-30-1999||01:47 AM||||All facia's have side marker light and also front turn signall lights and thos are all interchaneable||||reg||6
Z||000005||Monkeyman||12-30-1999||03:04 AM||||Quick thinking, Tom! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||WKDFIRO||12-30-1999||03:48 PM||||I changed the front and back facias from GT style to Formula style. The only thing that I found in addition to having to have the "egg crate" switched over, the wheel wells are different. GT flare out a little more than the SE models. You can either scrounge around looking for GT wheel wells or just do what Pontiac did - Staple an additional piece of material to the existing wells. When I went from 85 to 87-88 Formula Facias I had to actually change the steel bumpers (I guess I could have just drilled but I had the parts available) since some of the holes were different, you probably won't have this problem. Just in case though.<P>Have fun!||||reg||10
Z||000007||Monkeyman||12-30-1999||07:53 PM||||WKDFIRO--Stapled?!!!  What's next?  Scotch tape in place of motor mounts? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
